  "id": "COMPOUND:23198 - PROTEIN:685",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide and Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform, as this compound is implicated in targeting multiple downstream pathways. Specifically, the compound is associated with 72 kDa type IV collagenase, which is a target of two distinct molecules: (2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-2-[(2S)-2-[(3S,5R,8R,9R,10R,12R,13S,14R,17S)-3,12-dihydroxy-4,4,8,10,14-pentamethyl-2,3,5,6,7,9,11,12,13,15,16,17-dodecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-17-yl]-6-methylhept-5-en-2-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol and Spongia-13(16),14-Dien-19-Oic Acid. Both of these molecules are targets of the Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform. This indicates that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of this phosphatase, potentially influencing its activity in cellular processes. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, suggesting a possible regulatory role for the compound in the context of phosphatase activity. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are similar across the different paths, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains uncertain without further experimental validation.",
